// Four tray-packing levels: the harder shape a pack has to fit. Named
// metadata (budget, goal) that means nothing to a crate-pusher, level names
// with spaces, and TWO extra grids over the same board whose dimensions
// differ from it — the vertical-divider grid is one column wider than the
// tray, because it describes the edges between cells rather than the cells.

pack puzzle

legend
  .  empty
  r  red
  g  green
  b  blue
  y  yellow
  p  purple
  w  white
  k  black
  s  stone
  i  ice
  W  wild
  X  divider

